      accessible: 'Waves in the ocean: there\'s no separate "wave-thing" apart from the water moving. There\'s no separate "motion" apart from the wave. And there\'s no hidden substance under the water either — it\'s water all the way down, and even that is just molecules interacting. Similarly, QFT says reality is just fields — no separate particles, no separate properties, no hidden stuff.',
      twoTruths: 'Conventionally, we talk about objects, their properties, and the "stuff" they\'re made of — as three different things. Ultimately, all three are interdependent aspects of the same dependently arisen reality. The three-way distinction is conventional shorthand, not ultimate truth.',
      commonMisconception: 'NOT nihilism. Saying nothing exists INHERENTLY is not saying nothing exists. Objects, characteristics, and substances are all conventionally real. They function, they interact, they matter. But none of them has independent, self-standing existence.',
